6. Other validations companies commonly implement
These go beyond simple Hamcrest and TestNG assertions.
Validation type	What you verify
JSON schema validation	Response structure, required fields, data types
Authentication	Valid token succeeds; invalid or missing token is rejected
Authorization	Users cannot access unauthorized resources
CRUD consistency	Created data can be retrieved, updated, and deleted
Negative testing	Invalid inputs produce expected 4xx responses
Boundary validation	Minimum, maximum, empty, and oversized values
Data integrity	Values match expected business rules
Pagination	Page size, offsets, metadata, next-page behavior
Sorting	Results appear in requested order
Filtering	Every returned record meets the filter
Contract validation	Response follows the agreed API contract
Database validation	API results match persisted database records
Idempotency	Repeated requests behave according to API requirements